From: TeamHarrisCali <34009957+TeamHarrisCali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:37:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: maximise / restore, resize with L + drag; terminal
 scroll bar

- Title bar: a third box (maximise, then restore) left of minimise and
  close; long titles stop short of the boxes.
- nanowm: maximise fills the screen above the taskbar (found as the
  root child titled "taskbar"), restore puts the window back where and
  as big as it was; a maximised window does not move. Resize: hold the
  right button (the DSi's L) on the title bar, or the bottom right
  corner, and drag: the corner follows the pointer by as much as it
  moved, as an outline, at least 60x40, within the screen above the
  taskbar.
- nxterm: a scroll bar at the right (arrows: 3 lines, above/below the
  thumb: a page) over the 200-line scrollback; follows a resize (new
  columns and rows, TIOCSWINSZ so programs get SIGWINCH, the cursor's
  line kept on screen); 40 columns by default to make room for the bar.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
